  "reason": "Existing evidence is nonexistent, so the first experiment should test a multimodal baseline to establish whether combining RNA and image data improves performance. This configuration uses pca_n2000 (a standard RNA encoder) and resnet50 (a standard image encoder) with simple concatenation fusion, which is a logical starting point to assess the value of multimodal integration without overcomplicating the design. It clarifies whether multimodal approaches are worth pursuing before exploring more complex configurations."  
